# Phase 1 — Redis Single-Node Baseline

## Redis Performance, Scaling & Failure Experiments

**Phase:** 1 — Single-Node Baseline
**Experiment:** Baseline #001
**Status:** ✅ Complete
**Date:** 21 September 2026
**Redis Version:** 8.0.5
**Node:** `cluster-master`

---

## 1. Overview

This phase establishes the **single-node performance baseline** for the Redis Performance, Scaling & Failure Experiments project.

The purpose of this experiment is to measure Redis performance on one physical machine before introducing:

* Kubernetes/K3s
* Multiple Redis instances
* Replication
* Persistence changes
* Increased client concurrency
* Different payload sizes
* Pipelining
* Node failures
* Network failures
* Scaling experiments

The baseline provides a reference point against which future experiments can be compared.

> **Experimental principle:** establish a controlled baseline first, then change one major variable at a time.

